                            <comment id="14612790" author="corneadoug" created="Fri, 3 Jul 2015 03:15:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Can&apos;t reproduce. It could be because you didn&apos;t have internet at that time, since fonts are CDN related.&lt;br/&gt;
Maybe this issue could be to change the fonts to local assets just like this was suggesting:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/incubator-zeppelin-dev/201506.mbox/%3CCAAeYHL309wwghNd7CYZmeruUbrEdrZw%3DZQKKy-Abq13RL_M63w%40mail.gmail.com%3E&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/incubator-zeppelin-dev/201506.mbox/%3CCAAeYHL309wwghNd7CYZmeruUbrEdrZw%3DZQKKy-Abq13RL_M63w%40mail.gmail.com%3E&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14613423" author="moon" created="Fri, 3 Jul 2015 19:50:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Can you verify without using grunt serve? &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I can not see correct font when i access web app. but if i use grunt serve, i can see correct font.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14613575" author="corneadoug" created="Sat, 4 Jul 2015 06:33:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I tried with both grunt build and grunt serve.&lt;br/&gt;
No problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the PR#56 changes the directory structure, you might want to make sure that you have a fresh directory (especially when you switch from branch with old directory structure)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I usually do a &apos;git clean -dxf&apos; but be careful, it will also flush your notebooks and local configuration (basically anything that is not on the repo)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14613958" author="moon" created="Sat, 4 Jul 2015 16:42:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I tried after cloning code to new directory. But the result is the same.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14614492" author="corneadoug" created="Mon, 6 Jul 2015 02:36:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Since I had the font installed on my computer, I couldn&apos;t see the problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The problem is:&lt;br/&gt;
Now that we have a lot of css files, cssmin is concatening them, but is not handeling the &apos;@import&apos; that needs to be on top of the .css file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m looking into solutions to fix it.&lt;br/&gt;
One of them could be to concat a separated .css files with font imports only, at the top of the main.css file generated.&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
